Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Limit alpha map refresh to unmanaged windows.

The full alpha refresh from 0138 also reaches managed layered windows.
On Hyprland/XWayland, Photoshop's panels then show a separate shadow
window and can lose interaction after switching focus. In an isolated
copy, removing only 0138 removes the extra outline; the panel remains
interactive in that run.

Keep the map-time refresh for unmanaged alpha windows, such as the
measurement and Smart Guides readouts that need it. Managed palettes and
their shadow owners retain their previous mapping behavior. The full
exposure and scaled-surface shape handling in win32u is unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -906,7 +906,7 @@ static BOOL X11DRV_MapNotify( HWND hwnd, XEvent *event )
         if (hwndFocus && NtUserIsChild( hwnd, hwndFocus ))
             set_input_focus( data );
     }
-    refresh_alpha = data->whole_window == event->xany.window && data->use_alpha;
+    refresh_alpha = data->whole_window == event->xany.window && !data->managed && data->use_alpha;
     release_win_data( data );
     if (refresh_alpha) NtUserExposeWindowSurface( hwnd, 0, NULL );
     return TRUE;
